[Event "Pirc Defense"]
[Opening "Pirc Defense"]
[ECO "B07"]
[Origin "Vasja Pirc (1940s)"]
[Side "black"]
[Tags "e4,hypermodern"]
[Difficulty "2"]

1. e4 d6 { The Pirc: Black lets White build a centre and plans to attack it with pieces and pawn breaks. }
( 1... g6 { [%name Modern move order] The Modern: the bishop goes to g7 first, keeping ...Nf6 flexible. }
  2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Nf3 Nf6 5. Be2 O-O 6. O-O Bg4 7. Be3 Nc6 { This transposes to the Classical Pirc main line. } )
2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. Nf3 { [%name Classical, 4.Nf3] }
( 4. f4 { [%name Austrian Attack] White grabs the maximum centre. }
  4... Bg7 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Bd3 Na6 { The knight supports ...c5 and can go to b4 to hit the d3 bishop. }
  7. O-O c5 8. d5 )
( 4. Be3 { [%name 150 Attack] White plans Qd2, Bh6 and a kingside attack. }
  4... Bg7 5. Qd2 c6 6. f3 b5 { Black's counterplay comes on the queenside. }
  7. Nge2 Nbd7 8. Bh6 Bxh6 9. Qxh6 )
4... Bg7 5. Be2 O-O 6. O-O Bg4 { Pinning the knight that supports d4. }
7. Be3 Nc6 8. Qd2 e5 { The central break: Black finally challenges d4. }
9. d5 Ne7 { The knight reroutes toward the kingside; ...f5 or ...Nd7 and ...f5 may follow. } *
